    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Air Quality and Control",
    "chapter": "Emissions",
    "topic": "Emission Factors",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Emission Factors (EF): Numerical values that represent the amount of a specific air pollutant emitted per unit of activity.</p>\r\n\r\nEmission factor (EF) = Quantity of Pollutant Released / Quantity of Activity or Process.\r\n\r\n<p>For a coal-fired power plant, EF for SO$_2$ may be expressed as kg of SO$_2$ emitted per megawatt-hour (kg/MWh) of electricity generated.</p>",
