    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Fundamental Principles",
    "chapter": "Population Projections and Demand Calculations",
    "topic": "Demand Calculations",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Population demand calculations are essential in various engineering and planning fields, as they help determine infrastructure needs, services, and resource allocation. Population growth is influenced by birth rates, death rates, immigration, and emigration. Socioeconomic factors, government policies, and urbanization also impact population growth.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Population demand calculations are crucial for determining infrastructure needs, including transportation, water supply, sanitation, and housing.</li>\r\n<li>Population growth can have environmental implications, including land use changes, resource consumption, and waste generation.</li>\r\n<li>Utilities, such as water supply, energy, and waste management, need to adapt to changing population patterns and demands.</li>\r\n<li>Demographic data sources include national census data, surveys, and vital statistics.</li>\r\n<li>Public services and facilities like schools, healthcare centers, and public transportation must align with population demand.</li>\r\n</ul>",
    "important": "",
