    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Health Hazards and Risk Assessment",
    "chapter": "Occupational Health",
    "topic": "Noise Pollution",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-8\">\r\n   <p>Noise Pollution is unwanted or harmful sound that interferes with normal activities, affecting the quality of life.</p>\r\n\r\nSources of Noise Pollution\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Transportation Noise: Roads, airports, railways, and traffic-related activities contribute significantly.</li>\r\n<li>Industrial Noise: Machinery, equipment, and processes in manufacturing and industrial facilities.</li>\r\n<li>Community Noise: Noise from recreational activities, events, and public gatherings.</li>\r\n<li>Construction Noise: Machinery and construction activities generate significant noise.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nHealth and Environmental Effects\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Hearing Loss: Prolonged exposure to high noise levels can cause permanent hearing damage.</li>\r\n<li>Stress and Sleep Disturbance: Noise can lead to stress, sleep disorders, and other psychological impacts.</li>\r\n<li>Communication Interference: Noise can hinder communication, affecting social interactions.</li>\r\n<li>Impact on Wildlife: Disruption of animal behavior, migration patterns, and communication.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center> <p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f4/300x0w%283%29.jpg\" style=\"width:500px;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:300x0w(3).jpg\">Chuck Kardous</a>, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
