    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Safety, Health, and Environment",
    "chapter": "Dose-response toxicity",
    "topic": "Noncarcinogens",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Noncarcinogens: Substances that do not cause or contribute to the development of cancer.</p>\r\n\r\nFactors Influencing Noncarcinogenic Risk:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Population Sensitivity: Consideration of vulnerable populations, such as children, pregnant women, and the elderly.</li>\r\n<li>Cumulative Exposure: Assessment of combined exposure from multiple sources of noncarcinogens.</li>\r\n<li>Duration of Exposure: Evaluation of both short-term and long-term exposure scenarios.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nTypes of Noncarcinogens:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Chemical Noncarcinogens: Include a wide range of substances such as household products, industrial chemicals, and certain metals.</li>\r\n<li>Radiation (at certain exposure levels): Some forms of radiation are considered noncarcinogenic within specific exposure limits.</li>\r\n</ul>",
