    "chapter": "Solid Waste Management",
    "topic": "Transportation of Solid Waste",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "Waste Collection Strategies\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Curbside Collection: Common in residential areas, waste is collected directly from households at the curbside.</li>\r\n<li>Containerized Collection: Waste placed in containers at centralized locations for collection.</li>\r\n<li>Roll-off Containers: Large containers used for construction and demolition waste or bulk items.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nSpecialized Waste Transportation\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Hazardous Waste Transportation: Strict regulations govern the transportation of hazardous waste to ensure safety and environmental protection.</li>\r\n<li>Biomedical Waste Transportation: Specialized handling and transportation for medical waste to prevent contamination.</li>\r\n</ul>",
