    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Water and Wastewater",
    "chapter": "Physical Processes",
    "topic": "Air Stripping",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Air stripping is used for removal of ammonia from waster water.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The conversion of Ammonium ions to gaseous phase and then dispersing the liquid in air, thus allowing the transfer of the ammonia from the watewater to the air.\r\n\\[NH_4^+ + OH^- \\rightleftharpoons H_2O + NH_3 \\uparrow\\]</li>\r\n<li>Addition of lime</li>\r\n<li>The pH must be greater than 11 for complete conversion.</li>\r\n</ul>",
