    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Probability and Statistics",
    "chapter": "Probability Functions, Distributions, and Expected Values",
    "topic": "Normal Distribution",
    "subtopic": "Normal Distribution",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"notes-image-container my-4 text-center flex flex-col items-center\"><center><img src=\"   https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/Standard_Normal_Distribution.png\" alt=\"Normal Distribution\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Standard_Normal_Distribution.png\">D Wells</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons<br/></small></small></center></div><p>Normal distribution has a perfectly symmetrical bell shaped curve in which Mean = Median = Mode<br />\r\nNormal distribution is also referred as Gaussian distribution. Population parameters such as height and weight usually follow normal distribution. A standard normal distribution is a special case of normal distribution where mean = 0 and standard deviation = 1.</p>",
    "important": "\\[Z = \\dfrac{x - \\mu }{\\sigma }\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10MBZb3FfsbphzJym9zkPWLzZiIGKo06G/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pP0J03Um4o38T8QRpfIegnVvzrUi15je/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1g599fL3xaLt9jTf5d82biRvhGX88DQwx/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
    "images": [
      "   https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/Standard_Normal_Distribution.png"
    ],
    "local_images": [],
    "video": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hpRLtyDcQ6KvFx8v2UHpSqoVIeXYtEGs/preview",
    "videoTitle": "Normal Distribution"
