    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Ethics and Professional Practice",
    "chapter": "Societal Considerations",
    "topic": "Life Cycle Assessment (LCA)",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) identifies, quantifies and evaluates the environmental impacts (inputs and outputs) of a product, service or activity, from cradle to grave.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Stages of Product Life Cycle:</b></span></h5>\r\n<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Introduction: This stage includes creating consumer awareness and developing marketing strategy.</li>\r\n<li>Growth: Product is widely available, production is increased</li>\r\n<li>Maturity: Competition establishes, market saturates, demand does not grow further.</li>\r\n<li>Decline: Technologies evolve, fashion trends change, competitors offer better products, consumer tastes change. As a result, sales keep dropping.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\" text-align= \"center\">\r\n     <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/60/Product_Life_Cycle_Management.png\" alt=\"Product Life Cycle Management.\" width=\"500\"><br/>\r\n<center><small><small>\r\n<a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Product_Life_Cycle_Management.png\">Tres West</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Variants:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>Cradle-to-Grave: Assessment from resource extraction (’cradle’) to use phase and disposal phase (’grave’). e.g. paper</li>\r\n\t<li>Cradle-to-Gate: Partial product life cycle from resource extraction (cradle) to the factory gate (i.e., before it is transported to the consumer)</li>\r\n\t<li>Cradle-to-cradle or closed loop production: Where the end-of-life disposal step for the product is a recycling process.</li>\r\n\t<li>Gate-to-Gate: Partial LCA looking at only one value-added process in the entire production chain.</li>\r\n\t<li>Well-to-Wheel: Specific LCA used for transport fuels and vehicles.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Five Steps of a Product Lifecycle (Cradle-to-Grave):</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>Raw Material Extraction</li>\r\n\t<li>Manufacturing and Processing</li>\r\n\t<li>Transportation</li>\r\n\t<li>Usage and Retail</li>\r\n\t<li>Waste Disposal</li>\r\n</ol>",
    "important": "",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><!-- <div class=\"w-full mt-2\"><div style=\"padding:56.25% 0 0 0;position:relative;\"><iframe src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/833004878?h=c838c6076e&amp;badge=0&amp;autopause=0&amp;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" title=\"Product Life Cycle\"></iframe></div><script src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js\"></script></div> --></div>",
