    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Engineering Economics",
    "chapter": "Capitalized Costs",
    "topic": "Capitalized Costs",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Capitalized costs are present worth values using an assumed perpetual period of time. Capitalized cost takes into account the time value of money. This means that future costs are adjusted to their present values using appropriate discount rates to account for inflation and the opportunity cost of tying up capital.</p>\r\n\r\nSome real life examples where capitalized cost concepts are used:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Stock Price: Let us say company gives constant dividend every year. In such case, price of stock (share price) is present value of a perpetuity.</li>\r\n\r\n<p>e.g, ABC Corporation gives $2 dividend per share every year. Assuming the dividend remains same, and the company exists forever. and interest rate is 8%, the stock price should be present value of all those infinite dividends.</p>\r\n\r\n\\[ P = \\dfrac{A}{i} = \\dfrac{2}{0.08} = $25\\]\r\n<p>In reality, if ABC corporation is being traded higher than \\$25, then the stock is overpriced, alternatively, if it is traded for less than \\$25, then it is underpriced.</p>\r\n\r\n<li>Scholarship Fund: A wealthy donor wants to donate X amount to a university. The university will give a scholarship in his/her name to a deserving student. Assuming that the scholarship amount remains same every year and the university exists forever, here too we can use the concepts of perpetuity.</li>\r\n\r\n<p>Let's say, the scholarship amount is \\$8000 every year and the prevailing interest rate is 5%, then the lump sum money to be donated, X, can be calculated as:</p>\r\n\r\n\\[ P = \\dfrac{A}{i} = \\dfrac{8000}{0.05} = $160,000\\]\r\n\r\n<p>The person should donate \\$160,000, such that the \\$8000 will be given every year as a sholarship forever.</p>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$P = \\dfrac{A}{i}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 231</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>",
    "important": "\\[P = \\dfrac{A}{i}\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1havLCPfQl5t3b131JVdJFztjgaLZexTp/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o4113njSMO4VwuUfyaQXwugJV3ChZ6h1/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a></div>",
    "images": [],
