    "discipline": "Environmental",
    "subject": "Fluid Mechanics and Hydraulics",
    "chapter": "Fluid Properties",
    "topic": "Common Fluid Properties",
    "subtopic": "Density, Specific Volume, Specific Weight, and Specific Gravity",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"notes-image-container my-4 text-center flex flex-col items-center\"><center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/Density_-_Kilogram_per_cubic_metre.svg\" alt=\"1 kg per cubic meter\" width=\"240\"><br/>\r\n\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Density_-_Kilogram_per_cubic_metre.svg\">nclm</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/></div><h5><b>Density:</b></h5>\r\n\r\n<p>The symbol (<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\rho\\)</span>) used to\r\nrepresent density with SI units of kilograms per cubic meter. This term\r\nis the reciprocal of specific volume.<br />\r\n<span class=\"math display\">\\[\\rho = \\dfrac{m}{V}\\]</span> For cylinder,\r\n$V = \\pi r^2 h$ whereas for cone, $V = \\dfrac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h$.<br/>\r\nFor pure water, the density is 1000kg/m<span class=\"math inline\">\\(^3\\)</span>,\r\nSea water density is slightly higher (upto 1035 kg/m<span\r\nclass=\"math inline\">\\(^3\\)</span>) due to dissolved salts. Oil is\r\nlighter than water, resulting in density less than 1000 kg/m<span\r\nclass=\"math inline\">\\(^3\\)</span>. Solid metals and Mercury has density\r\nwhich can be found out by multiplying specific gravity by density of\r\npure water.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5><b>Specific Gravity:</b></h5>\r\n<p>Specific gravity is the ratio of the density of a substance to the\r\ndensity (mass of the same unit volume) of a reference substance. Since\r\npure water is usually used as a reference, specific gravity of pure\r\nwater will be 1.<br />\r\n</p>\r\n<div class=\"center\">\r\n<p>specific gravity = <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\dfrac{\\mathrm{density\\ of\\\r\nsubstance}}{\\mathrm{density\\ of\\  water}}\\)</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h5><b>Specific Weight:</b></h5>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\gamma = \\rho g$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 177</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<h5><b>Specific Volume:</b></h5>\r\n<p>Specific volume is defined as the number of cubic meters occupied by one kilogram of a particular substance. The units are m$^3$/kg.</p>\r\n\\[v = \\dfrac{V}{m} = \\dfrac{1}{\\rho}\\]",
    "important": "Density:\r\n\\[\\rho = \\dfrac{m}{V}\\]\r\nShear stress:\r\n\\[\\tau =\\mu {\\dfrac {\\partial u}{\\partial y}}\\]\r\nShear Force:\r\n\\[F= \\tau A = \\left(\\mu {\\dfrac {\\partial u}{\\partial y}}\\right) A\\]\r\nKinematic viscosity:\r\n\\[\\nu =\\dfrac {\\mu}{\\rho}\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sVimK-Jh9ukJbKIM9_gb3zudQpw0y30V/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RgZQqcipjRLwiwAc3UyWk4-cWlDeZ4P0/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1enRmKxBjLE-hjlNf5SpP1STih2jFe-bU/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
